      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General may authorise, in writing, the provision of\nmaterial to the ICC if:\n\n(a) the ICC has requested the material; and\n\n(b) the Attorney-General is satisfied that:\n\n(i) the request relates to an investigation being conducted\nby the Prosecutor or a proceeding before the ICC; and\n\nAssistance to international courts and tribunals  Schedule 1\nLawfully obtained material  Part 1\n\nNo. 34, 2018\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and\nOther Measures) Act 2018\n\n(ii) if the material is or includes lawfully intercepted\ninformation or interception warrant information—the\ninvestigation is into, or the proceeding relates to, an\noffence punishable by a maximum penalty of\nimprisonment for 7 years or more, or imprisonment for\nlife; and\n\n(iii) the material was lawfully obtained in Australia by, and\nis lawfully in the possession of, a law enforcement\nagency.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Attorney-General may authorise, in writing, the provision of\nmaterial to the ICC if:\n\n(a) the ICC has requested the material; and\n\n(b) the Attorney-General is satisfied that:\n\n(i) the request relates to an investigation being conducted\nby the Prosecutor or a proceeding before the ICC; and\n\nAssistance to international courts and tribunals  Schedule 1\nLawfully obtained material  Part 1\n\nNo. 34, 2018\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and\nOther Measures) Act 2018\n\n(ii) if the material is or includes lawfully intercepted\ninformation or interception warrant information—the\ninvestigation is into, or the proceeding relates to, an\noffence punishable by a maximum penalty of\nimprisonment for 7 years or more, or imprisonment for\nlife; and\n\n(iii) the material was lawfully obtained in Australia by, and\nis lawfully in the possession of, a law enforcement\nagency.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-69a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-69a-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-69a-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-69a-ss-1-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1b94590c236dca9559ff750c294c6ca37d4732473f0e6086195542ce6c15c9cd",
      "skos:note": "The Attorney-General may authorise the provision of material to the ICC under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-69a-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "69A(1) Authorising provision of material obtained by law enforcement",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General may authorise, in writing, the provision of\nmaterial to the ICC if:\n\n(a) the ICC has requested the material; and\n\n(b) the Attorney-General is satisfied that:\n\n(i) the request relates to an investigation being conducted\nby the Prosecutor or a proceeding before the ICC; and\n\nAssistance to international courts and tribunals  Schedule 1\nLawfully obtained material  Part 1\n\nNo. 34, 2018\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and\nOther Measures) Act 2018\n\n(ii) if the material is or includes lawfully intercepted\ninformation or interception warrant information—the\ninvestigation is into, or the proceeding relates to, an\noffence punishable by a maximum penalty of\nimprisonment for 7 years or more, or imprisonment for\nlife; and\n\n(iii) the material was lawfully obtained in Australia by, and\nis lawfully in the possession of, a law enforcement\nagency."
    },
