    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-11",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "11 Application and transitional provisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-11"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.15",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendments made by this Part apply in relation to a request made\nto the Attorney-General by the ICC, a Tribunal or a foreign country:\n\n(a) on or after the commencement of this item; or\n\n(b) before the commencement of this item, if, immediately\nbefore that commencement, the Attorney-General had yet to\nmake a decision on the request.\n(2)\nThe amendments so apply:\n\n(a) whether the material requested was lawfully obtained in\nAustralia before, on or after that commencement; and\n\n(b) whether conduct, a crime or an offence to which the request\nrelates occurred before, on or after that commencement.\n(3)\nAn authorisation that:\n\n(a) was made, before the commencement of this item, under\nsubsection 68A(1) of the Telecommunications (Interception\nand Access) Act 1979 as in force before that commencement;\nand\n\n(b) was in force immediately before that commencement;\ncontinues in force (and may be dealt with) after that commencement as\nif it had been made under subsection 68A(2) of that Act as amended by\nthis Part.\n\nSchedule 1  Assistance to international courts and tribunals",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThe amendments made by this Part apply in relation to a request made\nto the Attorney-General by the ICC, a Tribunal or a foreign country:\n\n(a) on or after the commencement of this item; or\n\n(b) before the commencement of this item, if, immediately\nbefore that commencement, the Attorney-General had yet to\nmake a decision on the request.\n(2)\nThe amendments so apply:\n\n(a) whether the material requested was lawfully obtained in\nAustralia before, on or after that commencement; and\n\n(b) whether conduct, a crime or an offence to which the request\nrelates occurred before, on or after that commencement.\n(3)\nAn authorisation that:\n\n(a) was made, before the commencement of this item, under\nsubsection 68A(1) of the Telecommunications (Interception\nand Access) Act 1979 as in force before that commencement;\nand\n\n(b) was in force immediately before that commencement;\ncontinues in force (and may be dealt with) after that commencement as\nif it had been made under subsection 68A(2) of that Act as amended by\nthis Part.\n\nSchedule 1  Assistance to international courts and tribunals",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-11-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c6c54d29ef0ffcf9b77c0ec79e4570ce0125abc5200b2e479a67d12e21ad2a6c",
      "skos:note": "Application and transitional provisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-11",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "11 Application and transitional provisions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 15,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendments made by this Part apply in relation to a request made\nto the Attorney-General by the ICC, a Tribunal or a foreign country:\n\n(a) on or after the commencement of this item; or\n\n(b) before the commencement of this item, if, immediately\nbefore that commencement, the Attorney-General had yet to\nmake a decision on the request.\n(2)\nThe amendments so apply:\n\n(a) whether the material requested was lawfully obtained in\nAustralia before, on or after that commencement; and\n\n(b) whether conduct, a crime or an offence to which the request\nrelates occurred before, on or after that commencement.\n(3)\nAn authorisation that:\n\n(a) was made, before the commencement of this item, under\nsubsection 68A(1) of the Telecommunications (Interception\nand Access) Act 1979 as in force before that commencement;\nand\n\n(b) was in force immediately before that commencement;\ncontinues in force (and may be dealt with) after that commencement as\nif it had been made under subsection 68A(2) of that Act as amended by\nthis Part.\n\nSchedule 1  Assistance to international courts and tribunals"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-11-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
