      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.19",
      "values:originalText": "The Attorney-General may authorise, in writing, the Australian\nFederal Police or the police force or police service of a State to\napply for a stored communications warrant under section 110 of\nthe Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979 if:\n\n(a) the Attorney-General is satisfied that:\n\n(i) a proceeding is before, or an investigation is being\nconducted by, a Tribunal; and\n\nSchedule 1  Assistance to international courts and tribunals",
      "skos:definition": "The Attorney-General may authorise, in writing, the Australian\nFederal Police or the police force or police service of a State to\napply for a stored communications warrant under section 110 of\nthe Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979 if:\n\n(a) the Attorney-General is satisfied that:\n\n(i) a proceeding is before, or an investigation is being\nconducted by, a Tribunal; and\n\nSchedule 1  Assistance to international courts and tribunals",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-34a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-34a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "248e1fb4f484f767b33568ae177217ece8a32176401e500770f8fe91aeb2fad3",
      "skos:note": "Authorise application for stored communications warrant"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-34a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "34A Authorising application for a stored communications warrant",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 19,
      "values:originalText": "The Attorney-General may authorise, in writing, the Australian\nFederal Police or the police force or police service of a State to\napply for a stored communications warrant under section 110 of\nthe Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979 if:\n\n(a) the Attorney-General is satisfied that:\n\n(i) a proceeding is before, or an investigation is being\nconducted by, a Tribunal; and\n\nSchedule 1  Assistance to international courts and tribunals"
    },
