      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.29",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(3) The authorised officer must not make the authorisation unless he or\nshe is satisfied that the disclosure is reasonably necessary for:\n\n(a) the enforcement of the criminal law of a foreign country; or\n\n(b) an investigation or prosecution of a crime within the\njurisdiction of the ICC; or\n\n(c) an investigation or prosecution of a War Crimes Tribunal\noffence.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(3) The authorised officer must not make the authorisation unless he or\nshe is satisfied that the disclosure is reasonably necessary for:\n\n(a) the enforcement of the criminal law of a foreign country; or\n\n(b) an investigation or prosecution of a crime within the\njurisdiction of the ICC; or\n\n(c) an investigation or prosecution of a War Crimes Tribunal\noffence.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-63-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-63-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-63-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-63-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-63-logic-ltl-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "278d6aed80570439e74ea8dd8cf9c8c12ee706940b36b4a00798d2e713a6a59b",
      "skos:note": "Cannot make authorisation unless disclosure is reasonably necessary for specified purposes."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-63",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "63 Subsection 180A(3)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 29,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(3) The authorised officer must not make the authorisation unless he or\nshe is satisfied that the disclosure is reasonably necessary for:\n\n(a) the enforcement of the criminal law of a foreign country; or\n\n(b) an investigation or prosecution of a crime within the\njurisdiction of the ICC; or\n\n(c) an investigation or prosecution of a War Crimes Tribunal\noffence."
    },
