    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-34b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "34B Authorising an authorisation for the disclosure of prospective",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-34b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.33",
      "values:originalText": "telecommunications data\n\n(1) The Attorney-General may authorise, in writing, the making of an\nauthorisation under section 180B of the Telecommunications\n(Interception and Access) Act 1979 for the disclosure of\ninformation or documents if:\n\n(a) a Tribunal has requested the Attorney-General to arrange for\nthe disclosure of the information or documents; and\n\n(b) the information or documents come into existence during a\nperiod specified by the Tribunal, and which started on or\nafter the day the request was made; and\n\n(c) the Attorney-General is satisfied that:\n\n(i) a proceeding is before, or an investigation is being\nconducted by, the Tribunal; and\n\nSchedule 1  Assistance to international courts and tribunals",
      "skos:definition": "telecommunications data\n\n(1) The Attorney-General may authorise, in writing, the making of an\nauthorisation under section 180B of the Telecommunications\n(Interception and Access) Act 1979 for the disclosure of\ninformation or documents if:\n\n(a) a Tribunal has requested the Attorney-General to arrange for\nthe disclosure of the information or documents; and\n\n(b) the information or documents come into existence during a\nperiod specified by the Tribunal, and which started on or\nafter the day the request was made; and\n\n(c) the Attorney-General is satisfied that:\n\n(i) a proceeding is before, or an investigation is being\nconducted by, the Tribunal; and\n\nSchedule 1  Assistance to international courts and tribunals",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-34b-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-34b-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e2a573a891a4566ec289772117e85e2506477f2dce97c86c69ac006cda5137b6",
      "skos:note": "Attorney-General may authorise disclosure of information or documents under specified conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-34b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "34B Authorising an authorisation for the disclosure of prospective",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 33,
      "values:originalText": "telecommunications data\n\n(1) The Attorney-General may authorise, in writing, the making of an\nauthorisation under section 180B of the Telecommunications\n(Interception and Access) Act 1979 for the disclosure of\ninformation or documents if:\n\n(a) a Tribunal has requested the Attorney-General to arrange for\nthe disclosure of the information or documents; and\n\n(b) the information or documents come into existence during a\nperiod specified by the Tribunal, and which started on or\nafter the day the request was made; and\n\n(c) the Attorney-General is satisfied that:\n\n(i) a proceeding is before, or an investigation is being\nconducted by, the Tribunal; and\n\nSchedule 1  Assistance to international courts and tribunals"
    },
