    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-79a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "79A Authorising applications for surveillance device warrants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-79a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.37",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General may authorise, in writing, an eligible law\nenforcement officer to apply for a surveillance device warrant\nunder section 14 of the Surveillance Devices Act 2004 if:\n\n(a) the ICC has requested the Attorney-General to arrange for the\nuse of a surveillance device; and\n\n(b) the Attorney-General is satisfied that an investigation is\nbeing conducted by the Prosecutor, or a proceeding is before\nthe ICC; and\n\n(c) the Attorney-General is satisfied that the ICC has given\nappropriate undertakings for:\n\n(i) ensuring that the information obtained as a result of the\nuse of the device will only be used for the purpose for\nwhich it is communicated to the ICC; and\n\n(ii) the destruction of a document or other thing containing\ninformation obtained as a result of the use of the device;\nand\n\n(iii) any other matter the Attorney-General considers\nappropriate.\nNote:\nThe eligible law enforcement officer can only apply for the warrant if\nhe or she reasonably suspects that the use of the device is necessary\n\nSchedule 1  Assistance to international courts and tribunals",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Attorney-General may authorise, in writing, an eligible law\nenforcement officer to apply for a surveillance device warrant\nunder section 14 of the Surveillance Devices Act 2004 if:\n\n(a) the ICC has requested the Attorney-General to arrange for the\nuse of a surveillance device; and\n\n(b) the Attorney-General is satisfied that an investigation is\nbeing conducted by the Prosecutor, or a proceeding is before\nthe ICC; and\n\n(c) the Attorney-General is satisfied that the ICC has given\nappropriate undertakings for:\n\n(i) ensuring that the information obtained as a result of the\nuse of the device will only be used for the purpose for\nwhich it is communicated to the ICC; and\n\n(ii) the destruction of a document or other thing containing\ninformation obtained as a result of the use of the device;\nand\n\n(iii) any other matter the Attorney-General considers\nappropriate.\nNote:\nThe eligible law enforcement officer can only apply for the warrant if\nhe or she reasonably suspects that the use of the device is necessary\n\nSchedule 1  Assistance to international courts and tribunals",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-79a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-79a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b8e9ff4d914552545b626650d7026a03bc41c08d99d90c86f463719d0c4a1068",
      "skos:note": "The Attorney-General may authorise an eligible law enforcement officer to apply for a surveillance device warrant."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-79a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "79A Authorising applications for surveillance device warrants",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 37,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General may authorise, in writing, an eligible law\nenforcement officer to apply for a surveillance device warrant\nunder section 14 of the Surveillance Devices Act 2004 if:\n\n(a) the ICC has requested the Attorney-General to arrange for the\nuse of a surveillance device; and\n\n(b) the Attorney-General is satisfied that an investigation is\nbeing conducted by the Prosecutor, or a proceeding is before\nthe ICC; and\n\n(c) the Attorney-General is satisfied that the ICC has given\nappropriate undertakings for:\n\n(i) ensuring that the information obtained as a result of the\nuse of the device will only be used for the purpose for\nwhich it is communicated to the ICC; and\n\n(ii) the destruction of a document or other thing containing\ninformation obtained as a result of the use of the device;\nand\n\n(iii) any other matter the Attorney-General considers\nappropriate.\nNote:\nThe eligible law enforcement officer can only apply for the warrant if\nhe or she reasonably suspects that the use of the device is necessary\n\nSchedule 1  Assistance to international courts and tribunals"
    },
    {
