    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-112",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "112 After paragraph 23WJ(1)(ib)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-112"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.46",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\nAssistance to international courts and tribunals  Schedule 1\nForensic procedures  Part 7\n\nNo. 34, 2018\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and\nOther Measures) Act 2018\n\n(ic) if the suspect is being asked to undergo a forensic procedure\nbecause of a request by a foreign law enforcement agency\nresponsible to an international tribunal—the following:\n\n(i) the name of the international tribunal for which the\nrequest was made;\n\n(ii) that forensic evidence resulting from the forensic\nprocedure will be provided to the agency;\n\n(iii) that the forensic evidence may be used in proceedings\nagainst the suspect in the international tribunal;\n\n(iv) that the retention of the forensic evidence will be\ngoverned by the rules of the international tribunal;\n\n(v) that the retention of the forensic evidence will be subject\nto undertakings given by the agency;\n\n(vi) the content of those undertakings;",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\nAssistance to international courts and tribunals  Schedule 1\nForensic procedures  Part 7\n\nNo. 34, 2018\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and\nOther Measures) Act 2018\n\n(ic) if the suspect is being asked to undergo a forensic procedure\nbecause of a request by a foreign law enforcement agency\nresponsible to an international tribunal—the following:\n\n(i) the name of the international tribunal for which the\nrequest was made;\n\n(ii) that forensic evidence resulting from the forensic\nprocedure will be provided to the agency;\n\n(iii) that the forensic evidence may be used in proceedings\nagainst the suspect in the international tribunal;\n\n(iv) that the retention of the forensic evidence will be\ngoverned by the rules of the international tribunal;\n\n(v) that the retention of the forensic evidence will be subject\nto undertakings given by the agency;\n\n(vi) the content of those undertakings;",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-112-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-112-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a75a7f5876274ec7142e2686c6373670acd4674aa8ca4f33ecc6dcbd78f4d74e",
      "skos:note": "International tribunal request for forensic evidence",
      "dc:description": "Forensic evidence, undertakings"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-112",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "112 After paragraph 23WJ(1)(ib)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 46,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\nAssistance to international courts and tribunals  Schedule 1\nForensic procedures  Part 7\n\nNo. 34, 2018\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and\nOther Measures) Act 2018\n\n(ic) if the suspect is being asked to undergo a forensic procedure\nbecause of a request by a foreign law enforcement agency\nresponsible to an international tribunal—the following:\n\n(i) the name of the international tribunal for which the\nrequest was made;\n\n(ii) that forensic evidence resulting from the forensic\nprocedure will be provided to the agency;\n\n(iii) that the forensic evidence may be used in proceedings\nagainst the suspect in the international tribunal;\n\n(iv) that the retention of the forensic evidence will be\ngoverned by the rules of the international tribunal;\n\n(v) that the retention of the forensic evidence will be subject\nto undertakings given by the agency;\n\n(vi) the content of those undertakings;"
    },
    {
