      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.47",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nFailure to consent to forensic procedure—procedure requested by\nforeign law enforcement agency\n\n(6) The constable must inform the suspect (whether or not the suspect\nis in custody) that if:\n\n(a) the suspect is being asked to undergo a forensic procedure\nbecause of a request by a foreign law enforcement agency;\nand\n\n(b) the suspect does not consent;\nthe Attorney-General may be requested to authorise (under an\nauthorising provision) an authorised applicant to apply to a\nmagistrate for an order for the carrying out of the forensic\nprocedure.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nFailure to consent to forensic procedure—procedure requested by\nforeign law enforcement agency\n\n(6) The constable must inform the suspect (whether or not the suspect\nis in custody) that if:\n\n(a) the suspect is being asked to undergo a forensic procedure\nbecause of a request by a foreign law enforcement agency;\nand\n\n(b) the suspect does not consent;\nthe Attorney-General may be requested to authorise (under an\nauthorising provision) an authorised applicant to apply to a\nmagistrate for an order for the carrying out of the forensic\nprocedure.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-113-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-113-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f4faadbac8a5c6f53180475ad0f4ccf0bea3af5a0d31cd966b10907d714c0b05",
      "skos:note": "Inform suspect of forensic procedure request from foreign law enforcement agency",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-113",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "113 Subsection 23WJ(6)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 47,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nFailure to consent to forensic procedure—procedure requested by\nforeign law enforcement agency\n\n(6) The constable must inform the suspect (whether or not the suspect\nis in custody) that if:\n\n(a) the suspect is being asked to undergo a forensic procedure\nbecause of a request by a foreign law enforcement agency;\nand\n\n(b) the suspect does not consent;\nthe Attorney-General may be requested to authorise (under an\nauthorising provision) an authorised applicant to apply to a\nmagistrate for an order for the carrying out of the forensic\nprocedure."
    },
