      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.53",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\nchild has the same meaning as in Part ID of the Crimes Act 1914.\nconstable has the same meaning as in the Crimes Act 1914.\nforensic evidence has the same meaning as in Part ID of the\nCrimes Act 1914.\nforensic material has the same meaning as in Part ID of the Crimes\nAct 1914.\nforensic procedure has the same meaning as in Part ID of the\nCrimes Act 1914.\nincapable person has the same meaning as in Part ID of the Crimes\nAct 1914.\nparent has the same meaning as in the Crimes Act 1914.",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\nchild has the same meaning as in Part ID of the Crimes Act 1914.\nconstable has the same meaning as in the Crimes Act 1914.\nforensic evidence has the same meaning as in Part ID of the\nCrimes Act 1914.\nforensic material has the same meaning as in Part ID of the Crimes\nAct 1914.\nforensic procedure has the same meaning as in Part ID of the\nCrimes Act 1914.\nincapable person has the same meaning as in Part ID of the Crimes\nAct 1914.\nparent has the same meaning as in the Crimes Act 1914.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-135-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "be98e6eec2f20db768d05e3c110c936b6c687327aee929cb6663ee82114b11ff",
      "skos:note": "Definitions for forensic terms"
    },
    {
