    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-32b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32B Authorising application for carrying out of forensic procedures",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-32b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.55",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General may authorise, in writing, a constable to\napply under Part ID of the Crimes Act 1914 for an order for the\ncarrying out of a forensic procedure on a person if:\n\n(a) a Tribunal has requested the procedure to be carried out on\nthe person; and\n\n(b) the Attorney-General is satisfied:\n\n(i) that the request relates to a proceeding before, or an\ninvestigation conducted by, the Tribunal; and\n\n(ii) that the person is, or is believed to be, in Australia; and\n\nSchedule 1  Assistance to international courts and tribunals",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Attorney-General may authorise, in writing, a constable to\napply under Part ID of the Crimes Act 1914 for an order for the\ncarrying out of a forensic procedure on a person if:\n\n(a) a Tribunal has requested the procedure to be carried out on\nthe person; and\n\n(b) the Attorney-General is satisfied:\n\n(i) that the request relates to a proceeding before, or an\ninvestigation conducted by, the Tribunal; and\n\n(ii) that the person is, or is believed to be, in Australia; and\n\nSchedule 1  Assistance to international courts and tribunals",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-32b-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-32b-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-32b-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "38e57e6d3cffe4fbe9ed694e1ea5c95634ec34064058fc9ea3566952bb2bd26b",
      "skos:note": "Authorisation to apply for carrying out of forensic procedures"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-32b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32B Authorising application for carrying out of forensic procedures",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 55,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General may authorise, in writing, a constable to\napply under Part ID of the Crimes Act 1914 for an order for the\ncarrying out of a forensic procedure on a person if:\n\n(a) a Tribunal has requested the procedure to be carried out on\nthe person; and\n\n(b) the Attorney-General is satisfied:\n\n(i) that the request relates to a proceeding before, or an\ninvestigation conducted by, the Tribunal; and\n\n(ii) that the person is, or is believed to be, in Australia; and\n\nSchedule 1  Assistance to international courts and tribunals"
    },
