    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-32c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32C Providing forensic evidence to the Tribunal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-32c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.56",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General may direct a constable about how forensic\nevidence is to be provided to a Tribunal if:\n\n(a) the Attorney-General gave an authorisation to the constable\nunder subsection 32B(1); and\n\n(b) the forensic evidence resulted from the authorisation.\n\nAssistance to international courts and tribunals  Schedule 1\nForensic procedures  Part 7\n\nNo. 34, 2018\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and\nOther Measures) Act 2018\n\n(2) A direction under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Attorney-General may direct a constable about how forensic\nevidence is to be provided to a Tribunal if:\n\n(a) the Attorney-General gave an authorisation to the constable\nunder subsection 32B(1); and\n\n(b) the forensic evidence resulted from the authorisation.\n\nAssistance to international courts and tribunals  Schedule 1\nForensic procedures  Part 7\n\nNo. 34, 2018\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and\nOther Measures) Act 2018\n\n(2) A direction under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-32c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-32c-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2c1ce45e5692b074e33320d18ffcac8443b317e8f19b3c97d0eabbbb1e619dcb"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-32c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32C Providing forensic evidence to the Tribunal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 56,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General may direct a constable about how forensic\nevidence is to be provided to a Tribunal if:\n\n(a) the Attorney-General gave an authorisation to the constable\nunder subsection 32B(1); and\n\n(b) the forensic evidence resulted from the authorisation.\n\nAssistance to international courts and tribunals  Schedule 1\nForensic procedures  Part 7\n\nNo. 34, 2018\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and\nOther Measures) Act 2018\n\n(2) A direction under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-32c-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32C(1) Providing forensic evidence to the Tribunal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-32c-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
