          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-32c-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-32c-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "53fb2b9422be2ccdb177c7923beac5948280b62248cd742638263513eddece2c",
      "skos:note": "The Attorney-General must direct a constable on how to provide forensic evidence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-32c-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32C(1) Providing forensic evidence to the Tribunal",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 56,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General may direct a constable about how forensic\nevidence is to be provided to a Tribunal if:\n\n(a) the Attorney-General gave an authorisation to the constable\nunder subsection 32B(1); and\n\n(b) the forensic evidence resulted from the authorisation.\n\nAssistance to international courts and tribunals  Schedule 1\nForensic procedures  Part 7\n\nNo. 34, 2018\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and\nOther Measures) Act 2018"
    },
