    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-166",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "166 At the end of section 93",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-166"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the person fails to comply with the notice only because the\nperson does not provide information or a document within\nthe period specified in the notice; and\n\n(b) the person took all reasonable steps to provide the\ninformation or document within that period; and\n\n(c) the person provides the information or document as soon as\npracticable after the end of that period.\nNote 1:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matters in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\nNote 2:\nSections 137.1 and 137.2 of the Criminal Code also create offences\nfor providing false or misleading information or documents.",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the person fails to comply with the notice only because the\nperson does not provide information or a document within\nthe period specified in the notice; and\n\n(b) the person took all reasonable steps to provide the\ninformation or document within that period; and\n\n(c) the person provides the information or document as soon as\npracticable after the end of that period.\nNote 1:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matters in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\nNote 2:\nSections 137.1 and 137.2 of the Criminal Code also create offences\nfor providing false or misleading information or documents.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-166-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-166-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "16929f6bd136adc47084b1c90e1e82366fd5d34e1b8544cd349f663dc5c89410",
      "skos:note": "Exemption from subsection (1) under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-166",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "166 At the end of section 93",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the person fails to comply with the notice only because the\nperson does not provide information or a document within\nthe period specified in the notice; and\n\n(b) the person took all reasonable steps to provide the\ninformation or document within that period; and\n\n(c) the person provides the information or document as soon as\npracticable after the end of that period.\nNote 1:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matters in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\nNote 2:\nSections 137.1 and 137.2 of the Criminal Code also create offences\nfor providing false or misleading information or documents."
    },
