    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-99a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "99A Seizure of certain property or things found in the course of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-99a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.64",
      "values:originalText": "search\n\nA POCA search warrant in relation to a crime within the\njurisdiction of the ICC authorises an authorised officer, or a person\nassisting in relation to the warrant, to seize property or a thing\nfound by the authorised officer or person assisting in the course of\nthe search if the authorised officer or person assisting believes on\nreasonable grounds that:\n\n(a) the property or thing:\n\n(i) is proceeds of the crime that are not of a kind specified\nin the warrant; or\n\nAssistance to international courts and tribunals  Schedule 1\nProceeds of crime  Part 8\n\nNo. 34, 2018\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and\nOther Measures) Act 2018\n\n(ii) is evidential material relating to the crime that is not of\na kind specified in the warrant; or\n\n(iii) is proceeds of, or evidential material relating to, another\ncrime within the jurisdiction of the ICC in relation to\nwhich a POCA search warrant is in force; or\n\n(iv) is relevant to a proceeding in the ICC in respect of the\ncrime within the jurisdiction of the ICC; or\n\n(v) will afford evidence as to the commission of an offence\nagainst an Australian law; and\n\n(b) the seizure of the property or thing is necessary to prevent its\nconcealment, loss or destruction or its use in committing an\noffence.\nNote:\nSubject to paragraph 98(3)(d), the POCA search warrant also\nauthorises the things set out in section 228 of the Proceeds of Crime\nAct.",
      "skos:definition": "search\n\nA POCA search warrant in relation to a crime within the\njurisdiction of the ICC authorises an authorised officer, or a person\nassisting in relation to the warrant, to seize property or a thing\nfound by the authorised officer or person assisting in the course of\nthe search if the authorised officer or person assisting believes on\nreasonable grounds that:\n\n(a) the property or thing:\n\n(i) is proceeds of the crime that are not of a kind specified\nin the warrant; or\n\nAssistance to international courts and tribunals  Schedule 1\nProceeds of crime  Part 8\n\nNo. 34, 2018\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and\nOther Measures) Act 2018\n\n(ii) is evidential material relating to the crime that is not of\na kind specified in the warrant; or\n\n(iii) is proceeds of, or evidential material relating to, another\ncrime within the jurisdiction of the ICC in relation to\nwhich a POCA search warrant is in force; or\n\n(iv) is relevant to a proceeding in the ICC in respect of the\ncrime within the jurisdiction of the ICC; or\n\n(v) will afford evidence as to the commission of an offence\nagainst an Australian law; and\n\n(b) the seizure of the property or thing is necessary to prevent its\nconcealment, loss or destruction or its use in committing an\noffence.\nNote:\nSubject to paragraph 98(3)(d), the POCA search warrant also\nauthorises the things set out in section 228 of the Proceeds of Crime\nAct.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-99a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-99a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "21f13c8ee7cc43fade7abc40e3ef187215022cde3275bde2b48e3df74b332991",
      "skos:note": "Seizure of property or thing found during search is prohibited unless certain conditions are met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-99a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "99A Seizure of certain property or things found in the course of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 64,
      "values:originalText": "search\n\nA POCA search warrant in relation to a crime within the\njurisdiction of the ICC authorises an authorised officer, or a person\nassisting in relation to the warrant, to seize property or a thing\nfound by the authorised officer or person assisting in the course of\nthe search if the authorised officer or person assisting believes on\nreasonable grounds that:\n\n(a) the property or thing:\n\n(i) is proceeds of the crime that are not of a kind specified\nin the warrant; or\n\nAssistance to international courts and tribunals  Schedule 1\nProceeds of crime  Part 8\n\nNo. 34, 2018\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and\nOther Measures) Act 2018\n\n(ii) is evidential material relating to the crime that is not of\na kind specified in the warrant; or\n\n(iii) is proceeds of, or evidential material relating to, another\ncrime within the jurisdiction of the ICC in relation to\nwhich a POCA search warrant is in force; or\n\n(iv) is relevant to a proceeding in the ICC in respect of the\ncrime within the jurisdiction of the ICC; or\n\n(v) will afford evidence as to the commission of an offence\nagainst an Australian law; and\n\n(b) the seizure of the property or thing is necessary to prevent its\nconcealment, loss or destruction or its use in committing an\noffence.\nNote:\nSubject to paragraph 98(3)(d), the POCA search warrant also\nauthorises the things set out in section 228 of the Proceeds of Crime\nAct."
    },
