    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-40af",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40AF Applying for and making production orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-40af"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.76",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An authorised officer may apply for a production order under the\nProceeds of Crime Act 2002 in respect of the Tribunal offence that\nis the subject of the proceeds request, if authorised to do so by the\nAttorney-General under section 40AB.\n\n(2) Part 3-2 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 applies to the\napplication, and to any production order made as a result.\n\n(3) That Part applies as if:\n\n(a) references in that Part to an indictable offence or to a serious\noffence were references to the Tribunal offence that is the\nsubject of the proceeds request; and\n\n(b) subparagraphs 202(5)(a)(ii) and (c)(ii), paragraph 202(5)(e)\nand subsection 205(1) of that Act were omitted.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An authorised officer may apply for a production order under the\nProceeds of Crime Act 2002 in respect of the Tribunal offence that\nis the subject of the proceeds request, if authorised to do so by the\nAttorney-General under section 40AB.\n\n(2) Part 3-2 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 applies to the\napplication, and to any production order made as a result.\n\n(3) That Part applies as if:\n\n(a) references in that Part to an indictable offence or to a serious\noffence were references to the Tribunal offence that is the\nsubject of the proceeds request; and\n\n(b) subparagraphs 202(5)(a)(ii) and (c)(ii), paragraph 202(5)(e)\nand subsection 205(1) of that Act were omitted.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
