    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-40an",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40AN Applying for and making monitoring orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-40an"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.80",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An authorised officer may apply for a monitoring order under the\nProceeds of Crime Act 2002 in respect of the Tribunal offence that\nis the subject of the proceeds request, if authorised to do so by the\nAttorney-General under section 40AB.\n\n(2) Part 3-4 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 applies to the\napplication, and to any monitoring order made as a result.\n\n(3) That Part applies as if:\n\n(a) references in that Part to a serious offence were references to\nthe Tribunal offence that is the subject of the proceeds\nrequest; and\n\n(b) disclosing the existence or the operation of the order for the\npurpose of complying with a person’s obligations under\nsection 40AO of this Act were a purpose specified in\nsubsection 223(4) of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An authorised officer may apply for a monitoring order under the\nProceeds of Crime Act 2002 in respect of the Tribunal offence that\nis the subject of the proceeds request, if authorised to do so by the\nAttorney-General under section 40AB.\n\n(2) Part 3-4 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 applies to the\napplication, and to any monitoring order made as a result.\n\n(3) That Part applies as if:\n\n(a) references in that Part to a serious offence were references to\nthe Tribunal offence that is the subject of the proceeds\nrequest; and\n\n(b) disclosing the existence or the operation of the order for the\npurpose of complying with a person’s obligations under\nsection 40AO of this Act were a purpose specified in\nsubsection 223(4) of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-40an-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-40an-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-40an-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "33b516921a8c910483a61915c558a57e5889357f5f07e5a7c54c7d3600e70c54"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-40an",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40AN Applying for and making monitoring orders",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 80,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An authorised officer may apply for a monitoring order under the\nProceeds of Crime Act 2002 in respect of the Tribunal offence that\nis the subject of the proceeds request, if authorised to do so by the\nAttorney-General under section 40AB.\n\n(2) Part 3-4 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 applies to the\napplication, and to any monitoring order made as a result.\n\n(3) That Part applies as if:\n\n(a) references in that Part to a serious offence were references to\nthe Tribunal offence that is the subject of the proceeds\nrequest; and\n\n(b) disclosing the existence or the operation of the order for the\npurpose of complying with a person’s obligations under\nsection 40AO of this Act were a purpose specified in\nsubsection 223(4) of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002."
    },
