    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-40ap",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40AP Applying for and issuing search warrants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-40ap"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.81",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An authorised officer may apply for a search warrant under the\nProceeds of Crime Act 2002 in respect of the Tribunal offence that\nis the subject of the proceeds request, if authorised to do so by the\nAttorney-General under section 40AB.\n\n(2) Part 3-5 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 applies to the\napplication, and to any POCA search warrant issued as a result.\n\n(3) That Part applies as if:\n\n(a) a reference in that Part to tainted property were a reference to\nproceeds of the Tribunal offence that is the subject of the\nproceeds request; and\n\n(b) a reference in that Part to evidential material were a reference\nto evidential material as defined in section 4 of this Act for\nthe purposes of this Subdivision; and\n\n(c) the words “or section 40AS, 40AT or 40AU of the\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995” were inserted\nafter “this Act” in paragraph 254(1)(a) of the Proceeds of\nCrime Act 2002; and\n\n(d) paragraphs 227(1)(a), (b), (h) and (ha) and 228(1)(d) and (da)\nand sections 256 to 262 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002\nwere omitted.\nNote:\nSections 40AQ and 40AR of this Act also apply in relation to a POCA\nsearch warrant. Sections 40AS to 40AU of this Act also apply in\nrelation to property or things seized under such a warrant.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An authorised officer may apply for a search warrant under the\nProceeds of Crime Act 2002 in respect of the Tribunal offence that\nis the subject of the proceeds request, if authorised to do so by the\nAttorney-General under section 40AB.\n\n(2) Part 3-5 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 applies to the\napplication, and to any POCA search warrant issued as a result.\n\n(3) That Part applies as if:\n\n(a) a reference in that Part to tainted property were a reference to\nproceeds of the Tribunal offence that is the subject of the\nproceeds request; and\n\n(b) a reference in that Part to evidential material were a reference\nto evidential material as defined in section 4 of this Act for\nthe purposes of this Subdivision; and\n\n(c) the words “or section 40AS, 40AT or 40AU of the\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995” were inserted\nafter “this Act” in paragraph 254(1)(a) of the Proceeds of\nCrime Act 2002; and\n\n(d) paragraphs 227(1)(a), (b), (h) and (ha) and 228(1)(d) and (da)\nand sections 256 to 262 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002\nwere omitted.\nNote:\nSections 40AQ and 40AR of this Act also apply in relation to a POCA\nsearch warrant. Sections 40AS to 40AU of this Act also apply in\nrelation to property or things seized under such a warrant.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-40ap-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-40ap-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-40ap-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f85776cb887c2fe6b4d3abd130772cd4410405c9d15b9bc54137890b1d656851"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-40ap",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40AP Applying for and issuing search warrants",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 81,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An authorised officer may apply for a search warrant under the\nProceeds of Crime Act 2002 in respect of the Tribunal offence that\nis the subject of the proceeds request, if authorised to do so by the\nAttorney-General under section 40AB.\n\n(2) Part 3-5 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 applies to the\napplication, and to any POCA search warrant issued as a result.\n\n(3) That Part applies as if:\n\n(a) a reference in that Part to tainted property were a reference to\nproceeds of the Tribunal offence that is the subject of the\nproceeds request; and\n\n(b) a reference in that Part to evidential material were a reference\nto evidential material as defined in section 4 of this Act for\nthe purposes of this Subdivision; and\n\n(c) the words “or section 40AS, 40AT or 40AU of the\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995” were inserted\nafter “this Act” in paragraph 254(1)(a) of the Proceeds of\nCrime Act 2002; and\n\n(d) paragraphs 227(1)(a), (b), (h) and (ha) and 228(1)(d) and (da)\nand sections 256 to 262 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002\nwere omitted.\nNote:\nSections 40AQ and 40AR of this Act also apply in relation to a POCA\nsearch warrant. Sections 40AS to 40AU of this Act also apply in\nrelation to property or things seized under such a warrant."
    },
