    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-40ar",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40AR Seizure of certain property or things found in the course of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-40ar"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.82",
      "values:originalText": "search\n\nA POCA search warrant in relation to a Tribunal offence authorises\nan authorised officer, or a person assisting in relation to the\nwarrant, to seize property or a thing found by the authorised officer\nor person assisting in the course of the search if the authorised\nofficer or person assisting believes on reasonable grounds that:\n\n(a) the property or thing:\n\n(i) is proceeds of the Tribunal offence that are not of a kind\nspecified in the warrant; or\n\n(ii) is evidential material relating to the Tribunal offence\nthat is not of a kind specified in the warrant; or\n\n(iii) is proceeds of, or evidential material relating to, another\nTribunal offence in relation to which a POCA search\nwarrant is in force; or\n\n(iv) is relevant to a proceeding in the Tribunal in respect of\nthe Tribunal offence; or\n\n(v) will afford evidence as to the commission of an offence\nagainst an Australian law; and\n\nAssistance to international courts and tribunals  Schedule 1\nProceeds of crime  Part 8\n\nNo. 34, 2018\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and\nOther Measures) Act 2018\n\n(b) the seizure of the property or thing is necessary to prevent its\nconcealment, loss or destruction or its use in committing an\noffence.\nNote:\nSubject to paragraph 40AP(3)(d), the POCA search warrant also\nauthorises the things set out in section 228 of the Proceeds of Crime\nAct 2002.",
      "skos:definition": "search\n\nA POCA search warrant in relation to a Tribunal offence authorises\nan authorised officer, or a person assisting in relation to the\nwarrant, to seize property or a thing found by the authorised officer\nor person assisting in the course of the search if the authorised\nofficer or person assisting believes on reasonable grounds that:\n\n(a) the property or thing:\n\n(i) is proceeds of the Tribunal offence that are not of a kind\nspecified in the warrant; or\n\n(ii) is evidential material relating to the Tribunal offence\nthat is not of a kind specified in the warrant; or\n\n(iii) is proceeds of, or evidential material relating to, another\nTribunal offence in relation to which a POCA search\nwarrant is in force; or\n\n(iv) is relevant to a proceeding in the Tribunal in respect of\nthe Tribunal offence; or\n\n(v) will afford evidence as to the commission of an offence\nagainst an Australian law; and\n\nAssistance to international courts and tribunals  Schedule 1\nProceeds of crime  Part 8\n\nNo. 34, 2018\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and\nOther Measures) Act 2018\n\n(b) the seizure of the property or thing is necessary to prevent its\nconcealment, loss or destruction or its use in committing an\noffence.\nNote:\nSubject to paragraph 40AP(3)(d), the POCA search warrant also\nauthorises the things set out in section 228 of the Proceeds of Crime\nAct 2002.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-40ar-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-40ar-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "19c0c4c38e064e25d12df0e8573953e9cf237d1152f0e08203c989586b5417b4",
      "skos:note": "Seizure of property or things found during a search warrant is prohibited unless certain conditions are met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-40ar",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40AR Seizure of certain property or things found in the course of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 82,
      "values:originalText": "search\n\nA POCA search warrant in relation to a Tribunal offence authorises\nan authorised officer, or a person assisting in relation to the\nwarrant, to seize property or a thing found by the authorised officer\nor person assisting in the course of the search if the authorised\nofficer or person assisting believes on reasonable grounds that:\n\n(a) the property or thing:\n\n(i) is proceeds of the Tribunal offence that are not of a kind\nspecified in the warrant; or\n\n(ii) is evidential material relating to the Tribunal offence\nthat is not of a kind specified in the warrant; or\n\n(iii) is proceeds of, or evidential material relating to, another\nTribunal offence in relation to which a POCA search\nwarrant is in force; or\n\n(iv) is relevant to a proceeding in the Tribunal in respect of\nthe Tribunal offence; or\n\n(v) will afford evidence as to the commission of an offence\nagainst an Australian law; and\n\nAssistance to international courts and tribunals  Schedule 1\nProceeds of crime  Part 8\n\nNo. 34, 2018\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and\nOther Measures) Act 2018\n\n(b) the seizure of the property or thing is necessary to prevent its\nconcealment, loss or destruction or its use in committing an\noffence.\nNote:\nSubject to paragraph 40AP(3)(d), the POCA search warrant also\nauthorises the things set out in section 228 of the Proceeds of Crime\nAct 2002."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-40ar-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
