    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-40as",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40AS Return of seized property to third parties",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-40as"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.83",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person who claims an interest in property that has been seized\nunder a POCA search warrant in relation to a Tribunal offence may\napply to a court for an order that the property be returned to the\nperson.\n\n(2) The court must be a court of the State or Territory in which the\nPOCA search warrant was issued that has proceeds jurisdiction.\n\n(3) The court must order the responsible enforcement agency head to\nreturn the property to the applicant if the court is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the applicant is entitled to possession of the property; and\n\n(b) the property is not proceeds of the relevant Tribunal offence;\nand\n\n(c) the person who is believed or alleged to have committed the\nrelevant Tribunal offence has no interest in the property.\n\n(4) If the court makes such an order, the responsible enforcement\nagency head must arrange for the property to be returned to the\napplicant.\n\n(5) This section does not apply to property that has been seized under a\nPOCA search warrant because:\n\n(a) it is evidential material; or\n\n(b) it is property of a kind referred to in\nsubparagraph 40AR(a)(iv) or (v).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person who claims an interest in property that has been seized\nunder a POCA search warrant in relation to a Tribunal offence may\napply to a court for an order that the property be returned to the\nperson.\n\n(2) The court must be a court of the State or Territory in which the\nPOCA search warrant was issued that has proceeds jurisdiction.\n\n(3) The court must order the responsible enforcement agency head to\nreturn the property to the applicant if the court is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the applicant is entitled to possession of the property; and\n\n(b) the property is not proceeds of the relevant Tribunal offence;\nand\n\n(c) the person who is believed or alleged to have committed the\nrelevant Tribunal offence has no interest in the property.\n\n(4) If the court makes such an order, the responsible enforcement\nagency head must arrange for the property to be returned to the\napplicant.\n\n(5) This section does not apply to property that has been seized under a\nPOCA search warrant because:\n\n(a) it is evidential material; or\n\n(b) it is property of a kind referred to in\nsubparagraph 40AR(a)(iv) or (v).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-40as-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-40as-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-40as-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-40as-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-40as-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c4ab617f55a335c6782680b289722b158239adf207ae44cc6bc1e7e77670eb39"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-1-sec-40as",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40AS Return of seized property to third parties",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 83,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person who claims an interest in property that has been seized\nunder a POCA search warrant in relation to a Tribunal offence may\napply to a court for an order that the property be returned to the\nperson.\n\n(2) The court must be a court of the State or Territory in which the\nPOCA search warrant was issued that has proceeds jurisdiction.\n\n(3) The court must order the responsible enforcement agency head to\nreturn the property to the applicant if the court is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the applicant is entitled to possession of the property; and\n\n(b) the property is not proceeds of the relevant Tribunal offence;\nand\n\n(c) the person who is believed or alleged to have committed the\nrelevant Tribunal offence has no interest in the property.\n\n(4) If the court makes such an order, the responsible enforcement\nagency head must arrange for the property to be returned to the\napplicant.\n\n(5) This section does not apply to property that has been seized under a\nPOCA search warrant because:\n\n(a) it is evidential material; or\n\n(b) it is property of a kind referred to in\nsubparagraph 40AR(a)(iv) or (v)."
    },
