    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-6-sec-26",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26 At the end of section 270.10 of the Criminal Code",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-6-sec-26"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.110",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(4) In this section:\nfamily member of a person means:\n\n(a) the person’s spouse or de facto partner; or\n\n(b) a parent, step-parent or grandparent of the person; or\n\nSlavery-like offences and relevant evidence  Schedule 6\nRelevant evidence  Part 2\n\nNo. 34, 2018\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and\nOther Measures) Act 2018\n\n(c) a child, step-child or grandchild of the person; or\n\n(d) a brother, sister, step-brother or step-sister of the person; or\n\n(e) a guardian or carer of the person.\n\n(5) For the purposes of this section, the family members of a person\nare taken to include the following (without limitation):\n\n(a) a de facto partner of the person;\n\n(b) someone who is the child of the person, or of whom the\nperson is the child, because of the definition of child in the\nDictionary;\n\n(c) anyone else who would be a member of the person’s family if\nsomeone mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) is taken to be a\nfamily member of the person.",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\n\n(4) In this section:\nfamily member of a person means:\n\n(a) the person’s spouse or de facto partner; or\n\n(b) a parent, step-parent or grandparent of the person; or\n\nSlavery-like offences and relevant evidence  Schedule 6\nRelevant evidence  Part 2\n\nNo. 34, 2018\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and\nOther Measures) Act 2018\n\n(c) a child, step-child or grandchild of the person; or\n\n(d) a brother, sister, step-brother or step-sister of the person; or\n\n(e) a guardian or carer of the person.\n\n(5) For the purposes of this section, the family members of a person\nare taken to include the following (without limitation):\n\n(a) a de facto partner of the person;\n\n(b) someone who is the child of the person, or of whom the\nperson is the child, because of the definition of child in the\nDictionary;\n\n(c) anyone else who would be a member of the person’s family if\nsomeone mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) is taken to be a\nfamily member of the person.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-6-sec-26-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-6-sec-26-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f552a1e79bdc74d313b3f0f000e309faa363c9b81f8db6b9d0fb2b41f0dcea48"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-6-sec-26",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26 At the end of section 270.10 of the Criminal Code",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 110,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(4) In this section:\nfamily member of a person means:\n\n(a) the person’s spouse or de facto partner; or\n\n(b) a parent, step-parent or grandparent of the person; or\n\nSlavery-like offences and relevant evidence  Schedule 6\nRelevant evidence  Part 2\n\nNo. 34, 2018\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and\nOther Measures) Act 2018\n\n(c) a child, step-child or grandchild of the person; or\n\n(d) a brother, sister, step-brother or step-sister of the person; or\n\n(e) a guardian or carer of the person.\n\n(5) For the purposes of this section, the family members of a person\nare taken to include the following (without limitation):\n\n(a) a de facto partner of the person;\n\n(b) someone who is the child of the person, or of whom the\nperson is the child, because of the definition of child in the\nDictionary;\n\n(c) anyone else who would be a member of the person’s family if\nsomeone mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) is taken to be a\nfamily member of the person."
    },
