    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-11-sec-10aa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10AA Matters covered by the AusCheck scheme—background",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-11-sec-10aa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.127",
      "values:originalText": "checks in connection with major national events\n\n(1) The AusCheck scheme may, for the purposes of paragraph 8(1)(d),\nmake provision for and in relation to any of the following:\n\n(a) the giving to the Secretary of information, relating to an\nindividual in respect of whom a background check is\nconducted, that is directly necessary for the purpose of\nconducting the background check;\n\n(b) the criteria against which a background check is to be\nassessed;\n\n(c) the decision or decisions that may be made as a result of a\nbackground check;\n\n(d) the form of advice to be given to an individual in respect of\nwhom a background check is conducted;\n\nSchedule 11  Amendment of the AusCheck Act 2007\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and\nOther Measures) Act 2018\nNo. 34, 2018\n\n(e) the form of advice to be given to other persons about the\noutcome of a background check.\n\n(2) The matters referred to in subsection (1) may relate to:\n\n(a) all background checks to be conducted for the purposes of\nparagraph 8(1)(d); or\n\n(b) a specified class of background checks.\n\n[Minister’s second reading speech made in—\nHouse of Representatives on 23 November 2016\nSenate on 13 February 2018]\n\n(178/16)",
      "skos:definition": "checks in connection with major national events\n\n(1) The AusCheck scheme may, for the purposes of paragraph 8(1)(d),\nmake provision for and in relation to any of the following:\n\n(a) the giving to the Secretary of information, relating to an\nindividual in respect of whom a background check is\nconducted, that is directly necessary for the purpose of\nconducting the background check;\n\n(b) the criteria against which a background check is to be\nassessed;\n\n(c) the decision or decisions that may be made as a result of a\nbackground check;\n\n(d) the form of advice to be given to an individual in respect of\nwhom a background check is conducted;\n\nSchedule 11  Amendment of the AusCheck Act 2007\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and\nOther Measures) Act 2018\nNo. 34, 2018\n\n(e) the form of advice to be given to other persons about the\noutcome of a background check.\n\n(2) The matters referred to in subsection (1) may relate to:\n\n(a) all background checks to be conducted for the purposes of\nparagraph 8(1)(d); or\n\n(b) a specified class of background checks.\n\n[Minister’s second reading speech made in—\nHouse of Representatives on 23 November 2016\nSenate on 13 February 2018]\n\n(178/16)",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-11-sec-10aa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-11-sec-10aa-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bf5d7ebbb85e647036abba1905500d9ba05600441ce74a07635cc4ef03b6f672"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018#sch-11-sec-10aa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10AA Matters covered by the AusCheck scheme—background",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 127,
      "values:originalText": "checks in connection with major national events\n\n(1) The AusCheck scheme may, for the purposes of paragraph 8(1)(d),\nmake provision for and in relation to any of the following:\n\n(a) the giving to the Secretary of information, relating to an\nindividual in respect of whom a background check is\nconducted, that is directly necessary for the purpose of\nconducting the background check;\n\n(b) the criteria against which a background check is to be\nassessed;\n\n(c) the decision or decisions that may be made as a result of a\nbackground check;\n\n(d) the form of advice to be given to an individual in respect of\nwhom a background check is conducted;\n\nSchedule 11  Amendment of the AusCheck Act 2007\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and\nOther Measures) Act 2018\nNo. 34, 2018\n\n(e) the form of advice to be given to other persons about the\noutcome of a background check.\n\n(2) The matters referred to in subsection (1) may relate to:\n\n(a) all background checks to be conducted for the purposes of\nparagraph 8(1)(d); or\n\n(b) a specified class of background checks.\n\n[Minister’s second reading speech made in—\nHouse of Representatives on 23 November 2016\nSenate on 13 February 2018]\n\n(178/16)"
    },
